  "prefLabel": "Cor 101.33 Work release",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cor 101.33 “Work release” means a structured program where persons under departmental control live in a group setting under departmental control and work at regular jobs in the community, and which is characterized by increased freedom as the program progresses.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Cor 100) #7446, eff 2-6-01; ss by #12500, eff 3-23-18 (formerly Cor 101.30) (See Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Cor 100)",
